<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obizzo III d'Este</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1294–1352</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obizzo III d'Este was marquis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> from 1317 and lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> from 1336, strengthening Este rule over both cities. He acquired Parma in 1344 but, unable to defend it, sold it to Luchino Visconti of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1346. His son Niccolò II and later descendants continued the Este dynasty in Ferrara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obizzo-iii-deste.jpg" alt="Obizzo III d'Este" width="286" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obizzo_III_d%27Este2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
